WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.220
Strong reflection is grounded in evidence.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:07.135
Evidence can include facts, timelines, artifacts, logs, metrics, user outcomes,

00:00:07.135 --> 00:00:11.000
test results, peer feedback, customer behavior, incident records, or observed performance.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.205
Without evidence, reflection can become a debate between feelings and assumptions.

00:00:15.205 --> 00:00:19.000
Evidence does not remove judgment, but it gives judgment something firmer to work with.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Separating facts from interpretations is a core reflective skill.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
A fact might be that a deployment took forty minutes, three alerts fired,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.000
or a user abandoned a workflow.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
An interpretation might be that the release process is broken,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.230
the alerting is too sensitive, or the user was confused.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:34.480
Interpretations may be correct,

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.265
but they should be tested against the evidence before becoming conclusions.

00:00:38.265 --> 00:00:40.000
Feedback improves calibration.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Calibration means matching confidence to actual performance, accuracy, or likelihood.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000
A person may be overconfident because a past decision worked out,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.215
or underconfident because one visible mistake overshadowed many correct choices.

00:00:51.215 --> 00:00:53.960
Feedback from peers, users, mentors, systems, metrics,

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.990
and outcomes helps people adjust confidence without overreacting to one event.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:02.110
Hindsight bias can distort reflection by making outcomes seem more predictable after they

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.955
happen than they really were before.

00:01:03.955 --> 00:01:08.000
A decision can look obvious in review even if the evidence at the time was incomplete.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Good reflection asks what was knowable then, what signals were available,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000
what uncertainty existed,

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.460
and how future decisions can be better supported without pretending the past was simpler

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.000
than it was.
